From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:06:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-lenovo-q706f: add the Goodix
 fingerprint sensor

Describe the fingerprint sensor for the goodix-fp-spi driver: interrupt on
TLMM 23 (rising edge), reset on TLMM 26 (active low), supply switched by
TLMM 131 modelled as a fixed regulator fed from vreg_l7c_ts_3p0, and the
trusted application name "goodixfp". Values come from the stock overlay
(dtbo goodix_fp node) and the stock HAL (ta_name). The SPI bus (QUP SE14,
TLMM 40-43) stays with TrustZone through gpio-reserved-ranges.

TLMM 26 was claimed by audio4_1p8_supply through the spkr_1_sd_n_active
pin state, a WSA speaker-enable inherited from the Qualcomm reference
board. In the stock DT the only consumer of TLMM 26 is the fingerprint
reset; the cs35l45 amplifiers use TLMM 49 and 127. Drop the GPIO and the
pin state from audio4_1p8_supply and keep it as a GPIO-less always-on
regulator so the cs35l45 vdd-batt-supply references still resolve.

THIS CHANGES THE SPEAKER SUPPLY WIRING. It must not be used beyond a RAM
boot until the owner has confirmed left/right speaker playback with it.

Signed-off-by: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
---
q706f-notes:
  Origin: q706f port (new), values from the stock Lenovo overlay (dtbo goodix_fp)
          and docs/EVALUARE-AMPRENTA-2026-11-13.md sections 1 and 11.4.
  Licence: GPL-2.0
  Rebase onto 7.3.4: n/a (written on 7.3.4)
  WARNING: changes the cs35l45 supply wiring (TLMM 26 leaves audio4_1p8_supply).
           Needs the owner's left/right speaker test before any use beyond RAM boot.

 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts     | 70 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 63 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
index 0ac5ed69d..ea2ea43b0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
@@ -242,19 +242,62 @@ audio3_1p8_supply: audio3-1p8-regulator {
 		regulator-boot-on;
 		regulator-always-on;
 	};
+	/*
+	 * Placeholder supply for the cs35l45 vdd-batt inputs. It used to switch
+	 * TLMM 26 ("spkr_1_sd_n", a WSA enable inherited from the Qualcomm
+	 * reference board). On this board TLMM 26 is the fingerprint sensor
+	 * reset (stock overlay: goodix_fp fp-gpio-reset); the amplifiers use
+	 * TLMM 49 and 127. Kept as a GPIO-less always-on regulator so the
+	 * cs35l45 supply references stay resolved.
+	 */
 	audio4_1p8_supply: audio4-1p8-regulator {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "audio4_1p8_supply";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
-		pinctrl-names = "default";
-		pinctrl-0 = <&spkr_1_sd_n_active>;
-		gpio = <&tlmm 26 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-		enable-active-high;
 		regulator-boot-on;
 		regulator-always-on;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Fingerprint sensor supply: TLMM 131 is "fp-gpio-envdd" in the stock
+	 * overlay; the stock driver drives it high on open and never touches a
+	 * regulator. The rail behind the switch is assumed to be pm8150a l7
+	 * (the stock vdd-supply), shared with the touchscreen.
+	 */
+	fp_vdd: regulator-fp-vdd {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "fp_vdd";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3000000>;
+		gpio = <&tlmm 131 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		vin-supply = <&vreg_l7c_ts_3p0>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&fp_en_default>;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Goodix fingerprint sensor. Its SPI bus (QUP SE14, TLMM 40-43) belongs
+	 * to TrustZone (see gpio-reserved-ranges); only the trusted application
+	 * "goodixfp" talks to the sensor. "goodix,gf3626" is the only compatible
+	 * the driver matches; the real part number is not known yet.
+	 */
+	fingerprint {
+		compatible = "goodix,gf3626";
+
+		interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
+		interrupts = <23 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 26 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		vdd-supply = <&fp_vdd>;
+
+		firmware-name = "goodixfp";
+
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&fp_int_default>, <&fp_reset_default>;
+	};
+
 	usb_vbus_5p0: usb-vbus-5p0-regulator {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "usb_vbus_5p0";
@@ -1912,12 +1955,25 @@ mclk2-pins {
 		};
 	};
 
-	spkr_1_sd_n_active: spkr-1-sd-n-active {
+	fp_int_default: fp-int-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio23";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-down;
+	};
+
+	fp_reset_default: fp-reset-default-state {
 		pins = "gpio26";
 		function = "gpio";
-		drive-strength = <8>;
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+
+	fp_en_default: fp-en-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio131";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
 		bias-disable;
-		output-high;
 	};
 
 	cs35l45_1_irq_default: cs35l45-1-irq-default {
